    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #10897.\n\n`OpenAIDatasetConverter` raises `KeyError: 'content'` when aligning a raw `IterableDataset` whose assistant message has nonempty `tool_calls` and omits `content`. [OpenAI's assistant-message schema](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat/subresources/completions/methods/create) permits that shape.\n\nProcess the existing tool-call branch before looking up content. Other messages retain their content-field requirement. Tests exercise the real streaming `align_dataset` path, all four content states (missing, null, empty and text), and missing-content errors for ordinary messages.\n\nThe affected path is raw streaming message alignment. Standard Hugging Face JSON loading fills missing nested content with `None` and already works.\n\nRelated #10455 handles `tool_calls: null`; this fixes the separate case where nonempty `tool_calls` are present and the content key is omitted.\n\nValidation on CPU, Python 3.11.0, datasets 4.0.0:\n\n- `pytest -q tests/data/test_converter.py`: original converter 1 failed / 9 passed; patched converter 10 passed. The patched suite also passed with `--import-mode=importlib`.\n- Ruff 0.15.5 lint, format (312 files), license checks and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Changed-file pre-commit passed. All 11 hooks passed in a temporary worktree after normalizing the Windows `CLAUDE.md` symlink placeholder; that placeholder change is excluded from the PR.\n\nTests used `WANDB_DISABLED=true`, `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1` and `PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1`. The full model-dependent suite and training were not run.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
